  "consumerStatus": "All direct mixin consumers inherit the shared preservation path. This source inventory is not all-page company-device UAT.",
  "platformDifferences": [
    "Windows/macOS desktop close uses the existing Flutter exit callback, draft/unknown guards, a ten-second checkpoint bound, local logout and a bounded remote revocation drain. Minimize/focus/background is not logout.",
    "Desktop staff credentials are process-scoped; legacy persistent credentials are retired with their original issuer. Account history, draft storage and encrypted revocation queue remain durable.",
    "Web keeps per-tab sessionStorage and ordinary refresh. Browser tab restoration policies and offline immediate remote revocation are not guaranteed.",
    "Mobile keeps existing secure credential storage/background behavior. The shared session watch and owned notification apply.",
    "WPF candidate has separate native evidence and remains unaccepted for full ERP/Win7 target hardware."
  ],
  "commonImplementation": [
    "Raw HTTP expiry can no longer directly open a kick dialog. Only an accepted end of the visible login publishes a generation-fenced notice.",
    "Watch is cancellable, uses staff credentials during impersonation, never binds or invalidates StepUp, never extends idle, and does not occupy a page-read scheduling permit.",
    "Human input still renews active use through the existing me path. A missing watch endpoint uses an automatic three-second probe and retries watch after one minute.",
    "Normal draft saves and retired-owner preservation share _commitLocalDraft and the same physical CAS/history/reset storage.",
    "Retired preservation never changes frozen request IDs, weakens stored Unknown or revives completed/deleted drafts. Conflicts use history-only RETIRED records and existing white-list projection.",
    "Client-release metadata-only/raw-CAS lease policy is retained, using the same physical FormDraftStorage CAS/history/reset implementation."
  ],
